  "notes": [
    "gatingActive = consent.require || consent.default === 'denied'. Inactive → every event enqueues immediately with consent merely attached.",
    "Active + unresolved → FIFO buffer capped at maxBufferedEvents (drop NEWEST, callback error '[SDK] Event dropped: pre-consent buffer full'); resolved granted → apply side effects (userId persistence), patch missing userId, enqueue; resolved denied → callback error '[SDK] Dropped <type>: no <signal> consent' ('identity update' for setUserIdentities: '[SDK] Identities dropped: no identify consent').",
    "The default timer (cmpTimeoutMs, 10000 default) resolves with consent.default when nothing else answers; a reset() re-arms it.",
    "`enqueued` lists what reached the transport in order, with only type/event/name/userId/context.consent/context.identities. callbacks[id] = null on success, else the error message. `reload` = new client over the same storage (hydration, source 'storage'). Runners map 'screen' 1:1; web 'page' is not used here.",
    "TCF/__tcfapi timing cases are browser-only and covered per platform by native tests (see tcf.vectors.json for the translation contract)."
  ],
